<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huang Jinrong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1868–1953</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huang Jinrong was a Chinese detective and gang boss who served for decades as a senior officer of the French Concession police in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a> while running opium, gambling and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> businesses. A leading figure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/green-gang">Green Gang</a>, he was the patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/du-yuesheng">Du Yuesheng</a> and helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a>'s purge of the communists in 1927. He stayed in Shanghai after 1949 and died there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huang-jinrong.jpg" alt="Huang Jinrong" width="300" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huang_Jinyong.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
